From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Petersen <ispeters@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 5 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] diag: name the concept whose args are read in the window

Not for upstream.  Instrumentation only.  Applies on top of 0005 (needs
the ArgsPopulated bit); independent of 0006.

ImplicitConceptSpecializationDecl holds only NumTemplateArgs and its
trailing array -- it has no pointer back to the ConceptDecl it specializes
-- so noteUnpopulatedRead() cannot name the concept.  The
ConceptSpecializationExpr can: it owns both the ConceptReference and the
SpecDecl.  Report from there instead, on exactly the event the ics-window
probe counts.  The decl pointer is printed so the two can be correlated.

  CLANG_ICS_WINDOW_NAMES=1 -> one "[ics-name] concept=... decl=..." line per
                              in-window read

No source location: StmtProfiler's base class carries only the
FoldingSetNodeID and two flags, with no ASTContext or SourceManager to
print one against, and plumbing one in is not worth it for a throwaway
patch.  The concept name is enough to find the declaration by hand.

The point is to identify which of stdexec's concepts are involved without
reducing the module interface, which needs two compiles per cvise test and
a preprocessed .cppm that may not round-trip.

Adds a public hasPopulatedArgs() accessor, since StmtProfiler is not a
friend of the decl.

NOTE: paths in this diff are relative to the `clang/` subdirectory of the
llvm-project monorepo, to match this repo's clang derivation's sourceRoot
(clang-src-.../clang).
---
--- a/include/clang/AST/DeclTemplate.h
+++ b/include/clang/AST/DeclTemplate.h
@@ -3270,6 +3270,10 @@
   }
   void setTemplateArguments(ArrayRef<TemplateArgument> Converted);
 
+  /// DIAGNOSTIC (not for upstream): false between CreateDeserialized() and
+  /// setTemplateArguments().  Public so StmtProfiler can name the concept.
+  bool hasPopulatedArgs() const { return ArgsPopulated; }
+
   static bool classofKind(Kind K) { return K == ImplicitConceptSpecialization; }
   static bool classof(const Decl *D) { return classofKind(D->getKind()); }
 
--- a/lib/AST/StmtProfile.cpp
+++ b/lib/AST/StmtProfile.cpp
@@ -22,6 +22,8 @@
 #include "clang/AST/OpenMPClause.h"
 #include "clang/AST/StmtVisitor.h"
 #include "llvm/ADT/FoldingSet.h"
+#include "llvm/Support/raw_ostream.h"
+#include <cstdlib>
 using namespace clang;
 
 namespace {
@@ -1764,6 +1766,22 @@
                                            const ConceptSpecializationExpr *S) {
   VisitExpr(S);
   VisitDecl(S->getNamedConcept());
+
+  // DIAGNOSTIC (not for upstream).  The ImplicitConceptSpecializationDecl has
+  // no back-pointer to its concept, so the name has to be reported from here,
+  // where the ConceptSpecializationExpr is in hand.  Fires on exactly the same
+  // event the ics-window probe counts; the decl pointer correlates the two.
+  //
+  // StmtProfiler carries no ASTContext or SourceManager, so no source location
+  // is printed -- the concept's name is enough to locate it by hand.
+  if (!S->getSpecializationDecl()->hasPopulatedArgs() &&
+      std::getenv("CLANG_ICS_WINDOW_NAMES")) {
+    const auto *D = S->getSpecializationDecl();
+    llvm::errs() << "[ics-name] concept=" << S->getNamedConcept()->getName()
+                 << " decl=" << (const void *)D
+                 << " nargs=" << D->getTemplateArguments().size() << "\n";
+  }
+
   for (const TemplateArgument &Arg : S->getTemplateArguments())
     VisitTemplateArgument(Arg);
 }
